Raman Spectroscopy for Mineral Identification — Bartholomew and Post (@mp-raman: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_3TQHZH1T2CDCQPTVVXSKJ5DCED
Paul R. Bartholomew and Jeffrey E. Post. Raman Spectroscopy for Mineral Identification: A Practical Guide, version 1.0, August 2024, 96 PDF pages. [MSA's authorized complete guide](https://msaweb.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/RSMI-Practical-Guide-2024-Proof.pdf).

Read the whole guide: physical principles, intensity/peak behavior, instrument performance, fluorescence, mixtures, weak signals, laser alteration, collection, processing, identification, database comparison, and solid-solution calibration. Its named practical sections support increasingly focused assignments; identification confidence depends on specimen/instrument context as well as a match score.

The publisher-hosted PDF and contents were accessible. Preserve the guide's actual rights, version, and component credits; free access is not asserted to be an unrestricted adaptation licence. Authors, date, version, scope, and source checked on 29 October 2026. PDF, spectra, and software remain external.

